The acl argument in the aws_s3_bucket resource is deprecated in AWS provider v4+ and was removed in v5. 
Since your provider is v5.91.0 (as shown in your provider.tf), you need to remove acl = "private" and use the separate aws_s3_bucket_acl resource if needed. 
However, since the task only asks to enable versioning, you just need to add the aws_s3_bucket_versioning resource.

Here is your updated /home/bob/terraform/main.tf:

hcl
resource "aws_s3_bucket" "s3_ran_bucket" {
  bucket = "nautilus-s3-753501112"

  tags = {
    Name = "nautilus-s3-753501112"
  }
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket_versioning" "s3_ran_bucket_versioning" {
  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.s3_ran_bucket.id

  versioning_configuration {
    status = "Enabled"
  }
}
💡 Key Changes
Removed acl = "private": This argument is no longer supported in AWS provider v5. 
If you need a private ACL, you'd use a separate aws_s3_bucket_acl resource — but the task doesn't require it, and buckets are private by default.

Added aws_s3_bucket_versioning: This is the correct resource for enabling versioning in provider v5+. The versioning_configuration block with status = "Enabled" turns versioning on.

Reference: bucket = aws_s3_bucket.s3_ran_bucket.id creates a clean dependency chain.

